# Cursor rules — The Reference Room

This project's canonical agent guide is **AGENTS.md** at the repo root. Read
that file first; everything below is a summary of the hard rules so they're
always in the system prompt.

## Project shape
- One static `index.html` (vanilla JS, no build) is the entire app.
- Optional Cloudflare Worker in `worker/` (image proxy + KV shared sets).
- localStorage for personal state. No backend otherwise.

## Hard rules — never violate

1. **No AI / LLM / semantic-search features.** The owner has explicitly opted
   out. The command palette is deterministic fuzzy matching plus rule-based
   keyword → filter mapping. Do not introduce model calls, embeddings,
   "smart suggestions" backed by an LLM, or anything that talks to an AI
   service from the client.
2. **Single HTML file, vanilla JS.** No build pipeline. Alpine.js or htmx are
   OK only if reactivity becomes painful. **No React / Vue / Svelte.**
3. **Preserve all localStorage keys** on every change. Schema lives in
   `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`. If you must migrate, bump `refhub_schema_v`.
4. **API keys never in client HTML.** Only in the Worker (`.dev.vars` locally,
   `wrangler secret` in production). `.dev.vars` is gitignored.
5. **Mobile-first, on-set 4G reliability.** Lazy-load embeds, inline what
   you can, avoid blocking external scripts.
6. **Don't add**: accounts, auth, real-time collab, Instagram embeds,
   tutorial modals, density toggles, more theme variants.

## Visual conventions
- Dark `#0E0E0F` base by default; **one** amber accent `#C8841C` → `#E5A042`.
- DM Serif Display for titles + section headers; DM Mono everywhere else.
- Hairline borders at 12–16% white opacity. **No drop shadows.**
- 8px grid, 24–32px section spacing.

## Where to make changes
- Visual / CSS → `index.html` `<style>` block (tokens + the "2026 REFRESH"
  override section near the bottom).
- Card copy → static HTML in body of `index.html` (`.card[data-anchor]` +
  matching `.detail[data-anchor]`). **Don't rename `data-anchor` values** —
  they're URL slugs and localStorage keys.
- Filters / roles → `FILTER_DIMS`, `ROLES` constants in the JS.
- New UX behaviour → end of the script block, follow the IIFE pattern.
  Wrap `window.openCard` etc. — bare-name calls bypass wrappers.
- Worker → `worker/index.js`.

## Before committing
Run:
```
node tests/smoke.js
node tests/logic.test.js
node --check worker/index.js
```
Then a manual browser pass (open a card, change a filter, copy a link,
reload, verify state restores). Don't commit if smoke or logic tests fail.

## Workflow
- `git pull` before starting, `git push` before stopping.
- One concern per commit. Clear "why" in the message.
- See `AGENTS.md` for the full multi-agent etiquette.
